The feathers of flightless birds also provide insight into their evolution.
Dinosaurs did not have a well-developed patella, known as the "raxis," in their legs; however, since their legs possessed other distinctive features—such as a kneecap and hair-like structures—researchers concluded that the raxis likely evolved later in evolutionary development compared to these other traits.
