Great changes have taken place worldwide due to humanity's scientific and technological achievements, and the growing population, along with humanity's extravagant lifestyle, has further intensified these problems, which is evident to everyone.
After being passed by Congress on July 4th, the handwritten copy signed by Congress President John Hancock and Clerk Charles Thomson was later sent to John Dunlap's print shop, located several blocks away.
