On July 8th, the document was read aloud to the public for the first time in the courtyard of the Independence Hall by John Nixon.
One of them was sent to George Washington on July 6th and read aloud to the troops in New York on July 9th. One copy arrived in London on August 10th.
The 25 known surviving Dunlap plates represent the oldest surviving copy of the document. The original manuscript has not survived.
