Because Auckland is surrounded by two harbors, it has numerous beaches. The most famous ones are located in three areas.
The Northern Beaches, located in the Northern Harbour district, are situated along the Pacific Ocean, stretching from Long Bay in the north to Devenport in the south.
They are sandy beaches, almost like a flat plain, safe from erosion, and mostly shaded by pohutukava trees.
The Tamaki Drive beaches are located along the prestigious waterfronts of the Mission Bay and Saint Heliers suburbs in Central Auckland, nestled within the Waitemata Harbour.
These are family beaches with occasionally crowded rows of shops lining the shoreline. Swimming is safe.
